# Supabase: Explicit GRANTs required for new tables

From October 30, 2026, new tables in the `public` schema are NOT automatically exposed to the Data API. Any new table needs explicit `GRANT` statements before `supabase-js` or PostgREST can access it.

When creating a new table in a migration, always include:

```sql
grant select on public.new_table to anon;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.new_table to authenticated;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.new_table to service_role;
```

Existing tables (guesses, profiles, mysteries, seasons, season_members, app_settings, etc.) already have implicit grants and are unaffected.
